0,Music of Vietnam - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_Vietnam,"Overseas music also called Vietnamese diaspora music, refers to the Vietnamese music brought overseas, especially to the United States and France by the forced migration of Vietnamese artists after the Fall of Saigon in 1975.",Vietnamese,Austro-Asiatic
1,Austroasiatic languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Austroasiatic_languages,"Languages in the Pearic branch and some in the Vietic branch can have a three- or even four-way voicing contrast. However, some Austroasiatic languages have lost the register contrast by evolving more diphthongs or in a few cases, such as Vietnamese, tonogenesis.",Vietnamese,Austro-Asiatic
2,AUSTROASIATIC: VIETNAMESE & HO (MUNDA) - YouTubeAn Updated Overview of the Austroasiatic Components of VietnameseAn Updated Overview of the Austroasiatic Components of VietnameseMusic of Vietnam - WikipediaAUSTROASIATIC: VIETNAMESE & EASTERN BRUU - YouTubeAustroasiatic languages - WikipediaVietnamese Music: From Traditional & Folk to Modern Sounds,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NR-iAlNkIaU,"Nov 24, 2024 · Let's learn different languages/dialects together. Vietnamese is the official language of Vietnam... Dec 17, 2024 · Despite the Chinese-like features of Vietnamese, Vietnamese still has core Austroasiatic elements at all linguistic levels, some of which can only be seen through reconstructions, but others which are much like pAA or any other modern Austroasiatic language. This study shows that, while Vietnamese is not a typologically characteristic Austroasiatic language, the Austroasiatic components of the Vietnamese lexicon and linguistic structure are more prominent than previously supposed. Overseas music also called Vietnamese diaspora music, refers to the Vietnamese music brought overseas, especially to the United States and France by the forced migration of Vietnamese artists after the Fall of Saigon in 1975. Mar 22, 2025 · Let's learn different languages/dialects together. Vietnamese is the official language of Vietnam... Languages in the Pearic branch and some in the Vietic branch can have a three- or even four-way voicing contrast. However, some Austroasiatic languages have lost the register contrast by evolving more diphthongs or in a few cases, such as Vietnamese, tonogenesis. Dec 20, 2024 · Traditional Vietnamese music, often performed with unique instruments, forms the foundation of this diverse musical heritage and continues to inspire today’s sounds. In this article, we explore the evolution of Vietnamese music, from its folk and court traditions to its modern, global appeal.",Vietnamese,Austro-Asiatic
